            'There were once two brothers in a Persian city: Qasim and Ali Baba. Qasim was a wealthy merchant, while Ali Baba was poor and worked cutting wood in the forest to sell in the market. Had Ali Baba not gone to the forest on that particular day, he would never have discovered the secret that changed his life forever.',
            'While Ali Baba was cutting wood, he saw a group of horsemen approaching, and hid up in a large tree out of fear of them. The horsemen stopped -- they were in fact forty thieves -- in front of a large rock. Their leader said loudly, "Open, Sesame!" and a secret door opened in the rock, and the thieves entered a cave full of treasure.',
            'After the thieves left the place, Ali Baba climbed down from the tree and remembered the magic word. He stood in front of the rock and said, "Open, Sesame!" and the door opened before him. Ali Baba entered the cave and found it full of gold, silver, and precious stones, so he took only one sack from it and went home.',
            'Ali Baba and his wife suddenly became rich, so they borrowed a scale from his brother Qasim\'s wife to weigh the gold. But Qasim\'s wife was curious, and put a piece of wax on the bottom of the scale to see what they were weighing. A small piece of gold stuck to the wax, so Qasim discovered his brother\'s secret and forced him to tell him everything.',
